In .NET 10 (starting with .NET 9 SR10+), `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` was deprecated on Android because the underlying `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` flag was removed by Google.

The recommended replacement is to use **`KeyboardAutoManagerScroll`** (enabled by default) or handle it manually with **edge-to-edge / WindowInsets**.

## Quick fix — let the auto-scroll manager handle it

By default in .NET 10, `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` is active. If it's not working, make sure you haven't disabled it:

```csharp
// In MauiProgram.cs – do NOT add this line (it disables the feature):
// builder.ConfigureMauiHandlers(h => h.AddHandler<Entry, EntryHandler>());
```

If you previously set `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust`, **remove it**:

```csharp
// Remove this — it no longer works:
// App.Current.Windows[0].Page.On<Android>()
//     .SetWindowSoftInputModeAdjust(WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize);
```

## If auto-scroll isn't enough (chat UI with pinned input bar)

Wrap your layout in a `Grid` and listen to keyboard insets manually:

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*, Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />
    <Entry Grid.Row="1" Placeholder="Type a message..."
           Margin="{Binding KeyboardMargin}" />
</Grid>
```

Then in your platform code (`Platforms/Android`), respond to insets:

```csharp
#if ANDROID
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

// In your page or a behavior:
var activity = Platform.CurrentActivity;
ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(
    activity.Window.DecorView, new InsetsListener(margin => 
    {
        // Update your binding
        KeyboardMargin = new Thickness(0, 0, 0, margin);
    }));
```

## TL;DR

| .NET 9 | .NET 10 |
|--------|---------|
| `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` | Remove it; rely on `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` (default) |
| Manual resize logic | Use `WindowInsets` API via `AndroidX.Core.View.ViewCompat` |

If `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` works for your layout (most cases), you just need to delete the old code and it should work out of the box.
